  "interpretation": [
    "Three decoded frames are submitted to the media compositor in one burst. The three SetCurrentFrame events span only 0.019ms; their media timestamps are 0, 52000 and 73000 microseconds.",
    "The first observed video frame callback follows the first SetCurrentFrame by about 13.7ms. The previous counter-at-three result does not by itself establish an extra two frame intervals of UI delay.",
    "The trace shows the first decoder request about 62.9ms before the burst, with three decoder outputs then released together. This locates a startup batch in this browser media path; it does not prove which decoder policy or source property caused it.",
    "The strict presentedFrames=1 gate remains failed, and no earlier failed trial is reclassified. Physical first visibility also depends on compositor submission and the loading overlay; this is not a physical display latency measurement.",
    "Other tabs appear in a browser-wide trace. Only the first, sole-reader trace is analyzed here; raw second-reader trace events must not be attributed without process/player isolation."
